# Frontend only, and only what is actually staged.
#
# Runs ESLint, not Prettier. Formatting is a separate decision that has not been
# taken yet (docs/backlog.md F1): this codebase is dense enough that Prettier
# rewrites about 2.3 lines for every line in a file it touches, so adopting it
# per-file would put a large reformat on top of every small fix.
#
# The backend is not here on purpose: ruff and black live in the backend venv
# and are not on PATH for most shells, so this hook would either fail commits
# over a missing tool — which teaches people to reach for --no-verify and
# removes the hook entirely — or skip silently and imply a check that never
# ran. CI runs ruff and black unconditionally, which is the honest place for a
# check that cannot rely on a local environment.
cd frontend && npx lint-staged
